  "domain": "machine-learning",
  "definition": "Differentiable rendering is a class of algorithms that reformulate the image-formation pipeline so that pixel values are differentiable with respect to scene parameters \u2014 including geometry, surface materials, lighting, and camera pose. By enabling backpropagation through the rendering process, these methods support gradient-based optimisation for inverse rendering, scene reconstruction from 2D observations, and end-to-end training of 3D-aware neural models. The field bridges classical computer graphics with deep learning, treating rendering as a learnable, differentiable module within a larger neural architecture.",
